/Title (The 0/1 Knapsack Problem was successfully solved using Dynamic Programming by building a table that considers, for every item, whether including or excluding it yields the better value. This bottom-up approach guarantees the optimal solution within the given capacity constraint. The algorithm runs in O\(nW\) time and O\(nW\) space, where n is the number of items and W is the knapsack capacity.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 218 0 R
>>
