/T (The 0/1 Knapsack Problem was successfully solved using Dynamic Programming by building a table that considers, for every item, whether including or excluding it yields the better value. This bottom-up approach guarantees the optimal solution within the given capacity constraint. The algorithm runs in O\(nW\) time and O\(nW\) space, where n is the number of items and W is the knapsack capacity. )
